cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DentDeID in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "DentDeID: open, tested de-identification for dental images"
abstract: >-
  DentDeID removes patient-identifying information from dental images: DICOM attributes following
  the DICOM PS3.15 (2026d) Basic Application Level Confidentiality Profile (rule tables generated from
  the standard), burned-in text (a dental-aware morphological detector with an identical JavaScript
  port), EXIF/GPS/XMP metadata and identifying file names of exported images and screenshots, faces in
  extra-oral photographs, and the facial re-identification risk of CBCT volumes. Every output is
  re-opened and re-checked, failures are quarantined, and audit reports contain no patient
  identifiers. It ships a Python library and CLI, a zero-install web application, and DentDeID-Synth,
  a synthetic benchmark with answer keys. Validated on synthetic data only.
